{
  "story_id": "S133",
  "title": "Ankrd11 and Setd5 converge on a thalamic synaptic receptor and channel program that opposes Med23/Wdr26",
  "status": "grounded",
  "rejection_reason": null,
  "exact_observed_result": "Ankrd11 was depleted in 151 TH and induced a synaptic/signaling subset containing Lrrc7, Ntng1, Grm1, Plekhg1, Prkcd, and Rgs4. Setd5 produced an overlapping 151 TH response with Adarb1, Rgs4, Prkcd, and Lrrc7 induced and Kat6b repressed. Restricted comparisons placed Setd5 as Ankrd11-positive and Med23/Wdr26 as inverse for several of these markers.",
  "biological_interpretation": "Two haploinsufficient chromatin neurodevelopmental genes converge on a thalamic membrane, synaptic, and excitability state that is not explained by generic chromatin-regulator or ankyrin-repeat family membership.",
